                <pb facs="0331" n="159" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg159"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857/388</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Southampton</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Swalm</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Southampton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1917-03-03T13:30:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1917-03-02T00:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received March
                            3, 1917, 1.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>British steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Belgier</hi> torpedoed February 23,
                    forty miles off Lauriat [<hi rendition="#italic">Lorient?</hi>], France, four
                    Americans in crew. Joint affidavit of Isadore Frank,
                        Leroy Kraig, DeWitt Shivers, and
                        Daniel Gatliff forwarded. Bound New York to French
                    port, cargo munitions. Vessel stopped by gunfire, German submarine. Weather
                    fine, French scout appeared immediately, took crew from boats, landed at Lauriat
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">Lorient?</hi>], sent here, no casualties, did not
                    resist.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Swalm</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
